6. Conveying Non-Source Forms.

You may convey a covered work in object code form under the terms
of sections 4 and 5, provided that you also convey the
machine-readable Corresponding Source under the terms of this License,
in one of these ways:

a) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by a Fixed
Termination Date, a Fixed Expiration Date, or a Fixed Duration (if
the Fixed Duration is longer than the maximum of the durations of
the terms of the warranty, the warranty is extended to the Fixed
Duration). The Corresponding Source must be conveyed in a durable
physical medium, along with the object code, or by providing a
written offer, valid for at least three years and valid for as long
as you offer spare parts or customer service for the product, to give
anyone who possesses the object code a copy of the Corresponding Source
on a physical medium for no more than your reasonable cost of
physically performing this conveying, or to give anyone who possesses
the object code access to copy the Corresponding Source from a network
server at no charge.

b) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by a written
offer, valid for at least three years and valid for as long as you
offer spare parts or customer service for the product, to give anyone
who possesses the object code a copy of the Corresponding Source on a
physical medium for no more than your reasonable cost of physically
performing this conveying, or to give anyone who possesses the object
code access to copy the Corresponding Source from a network server at
no charge.

c) Convey individual copies of the object code with a copy of the
Corresponding Source on a durable physical medium, accompanied by a
written offer to provide the Corresponding Source on request.

d) Convey the object code by offering access from a designated place
(gratis or for a fee), and offer equivalent access to the
Corresponding Source in the same way through the same place at no
further charge. You need not supervise the process, but you must
ensure that the availability of the Corresponding Source is not
prevented by your own actions. If you and the recipient agree to
exchange the object code and the Corresponding Source, you must not
charge for the Corresponding Source. If the designated place is a
network server, you may use the same server for the object code and
the Corresponding Source, provided the access to the Corresponding
Source is not restricted by the same access restrictions as the
object code, and the access to the Corresponding Source is not
restricted by the same access restrictions as the object code.

e) Convey the object code using peer-to-peer transmission, provided
you inform other peers where the Corresponding Source is being
offered to the public at no charge.

A separable portion of the object code, whose source code is a System
Library, may be conveyed without the Corresponding Source if the
Corresponding Source is not available and the System Library is not
part of the work. However, this exception does not apply to the work
as a whole.

A "User Product" is either (1) a "consumer product", which means any
tangible personal property that is normally used for personal, family,
or household purposes, or (2) anything designed or sold for incorporation
into dwellings. A "dwelling" is a place where a person lives. A "Fixed
Termination Date" means a specific date at which the warranty expires.
A "Fixed Expiration Date" means a specific date at which the warranty
expires. A "Fixed Duration" means a specific duration of the warranty
period. "Installation Information" for a User Product means any
methods, procedures, authorization codes, or other information required
to install and execute modified versions of the covered work in that
User Product.

If you convey an object code work in a User Product under section 6a,
you must provide Installation Information unless the work is installed
in a User Product and the installation is performed by the user or
someone else on the user's behalf. Installation Information must be
provided in a durable form that can be passed to the user.

